        "dimensions": [
          "syntax",
          "concept"
        ],
        "text": "today修饰需要决定的时间；to meet the deadline说明今天决定的目的，不直接给出deadline是哪一天。 今天作决定被视为赶上后续时限所需的一步。原句没有说截止时间就是今天，也未说明晚决定的全部后果。",
        "sourceRefs": [
          {
            "sourceId": "oewn-2025",
            "sourceVersion": "2025",
            "locator": "entries-d.json/deadline/n / deadline%1:28:00::",
            "supportedClaim": "the point in time at which something must be completed",
            "url": "https://en-word.net/"
          }
        ],
        "title": "句子结构与当前所指"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "contrast",
        "dimensions": [
          "contrast"
        ],
        "text": "deadline是最迟时限；target date是计划争取的日期；decision date是决定发生时间。在本句中今天的决定与最终期限应分开。",
        "sourceRefs": [],
        "title": "容易混淆的地方"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "game-neighbors",
        "dimensions": [
          "languageGame",
          "englishNeighbors"
        ],
        "text": "应核对截止事项、剩余步骤和决定依据；时限压力需要被明确表达，不能据此跳过必要核查。 meet/miss a deadline表示赶上或错过；extend a deadline指改变时限；decision today解释当前紧迫动作。",
        "sourceRefs": [],
        "title": "讨论通常怎样继续"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "action",
        "dimensions": [
          "pragmaticAction"
        ],
        "text": "说话者在强调今天作决定的紧迫性。",
        "sourceRefs": [],
        "title": "说话者正在做什么"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "workplace",
        "dimensions": [
